# LPR-016 (round-26): repository governance — required reviewers.
#
# CODEOWNERS pins ownership at the path level. When a PR touches a matched
# path, GitHub auto-requests a review from the listed owner(s) and
# (optionally) blocks merge until they approve.
#
# Syntax: <pattern>  <owner> [<owner> ...]
#   - The LAST match wins, so put the most-specific patterns first.
#   - Lines starting with `#` are comments.
#   - Use @adithya300800 for the current sole maintainer; if a future
#     @acs-portal-maintainers team is created, swap the placeholder.
#   - Use @acs-portal/security for security-sensitive paths so the team
#     that owns rotate-secrets / incident-response also blocks the merge.
#
# If `@adithya300800` does not exist as a GitHub user on this repo, replace
# it with a valid team handle (e.g. `@acs-portal/maintainers`) before
# enforcing branch protection on this file.

# ─── Default owner ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Everything not matched below falls back to the sole maintainer. This is
# intentionally broad — the explicit blocks below add additional reviewers
# without removing the default.
*       @adithya300800

# ─── Backend (production-readiness sensitive) ────────────────────────────────
# Auth, schema, and storage code touches identity, data durability, and
# cost. Require the backend maintainer for review.
/backend/src/middleware/        @adithya300800
/backend/src/routes/auth.js     @adithya300800
/backend/src/routes/storage.js  @adithya300800
/backend/src/lib/storage.js     @adithya300800
/backend/src/lib/uploadRoutes.js @adithya300800
/backend/src/index.js           @adithya300800
/backend/prisma/                @adithya300800

# ─── Frontend (auth-gated surfaces) ──────────────────────────────────────────
# The AuthProvider + RouterScope layering in CLAUDE.md is load-bearing for
# the round-17 (C-20) fix; any change to auth context, router structure, or
# the 401 interceptor needs the frontend maintainer.
/frontend/src/contexts/         @adithya300800
/frontend/src/main.jsx          @adithya300800
/frontend/src/App.jsx           @adithya300800
/frontend/src/layouts/          @adithya300800

# ─── CI / release pipelines ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Deploy workflows and secret scanning are release-blockers. Touching these
# without review has shipped data-loss bugs before.
/.github/workflows/             @adithya300800

# ─── Sensitive data paths (defence-in-depth) ─────────────────────────────────
# GitHub itself blocks commits to `.env*` only when the secret-scanning
# workflow catches a credential; this entry adds a reviewer as well so a
# typo'd secret in a tracked file gets caught before merge.
/.env*                          @adithya300800

# ─── Documentation that controls deployment behaviour ────────────────────────
# CLAUDE.md + the round-* memory files encode operational decisions; the
# reviewer check prevents accidental rewrites.
/CLAUDE.md                      @adithya300800
/docs/PORTAL_UX_AUDIT.md        @adithya300800
